        <body>
            <div xml:id="d559">

                <pb facs="0974" n="874" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg874"/>

                <head>No. 559.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hoffman to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-05-17"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 17, 1880</date>.
                        (Received June 5.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 208.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 205, in
                    relation to the case of Henry Pinkos, an American citizen and an Israelite, I
                    have the honor to inform you that I am at length in receipt of a note from Mr.
                    de Giers, in answer to mine of the 20th April.</p>
                <p>The Russian Government grants to Pinkos a delay of three months in order to wind
                    up his business.</p>
                <p>On sending to notify him I found that he was still at St Petersburg, the police
                    superintendent of his district having permitted him to remain from day to day
                    since the expiration of the time allowed him by General Zouroff to await the
                    answer of the Russian Government.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WICKHAM HOFFMAN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
